---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About Web Grouth | Risk-Free Guest Posting Network" description="Learn how Web Grouth combines a 40,000+ publisher database, human campaign support and a pay-after-live guest posting model.">
  <div class="saas-page">
    <section class="saas-hero">
      <div class="shell saas-hero-grid">
        <div class="saas-hero-copy" data-reveal>
          <div class="saas-breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>About</span></div>
          <span class="saas-kicker">About Web Grouth</span>
          <h1>A guest posting partner built around <span>clarity and delivery.</span></h1>
          <p>Web Grouth helps brands, consultants and SEO agencies secure relevant guest posts and contextual backlinks without paying before an approved placement is live.</p>
          <div class="saas-hero-actions"><a class="saas-button primary" href="/order">Start a risk-free order ↗</a><a class="saas-button secondary" href="/contact">Talk to Web Grouth</a></div>
        </div>
        <aside class="saas-hero-panel" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
          <span>Web Grouth at a glance</span>
          <ul><li>Publisher inventory <span>40,000+ websites</span></li><li>Primary service <span>Guest post placements</span></li><li>Payment model <span>After eligible live delivery</span></li><li>Campaign support <span>Single, recurring & bulk</span></li><li>Service coverage <span>Worldwide</span></li></ul>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-section">
      <div class="shell metric-row" data-reveal>
        <article><strong>40,000+</strong><span>publisher websites available across major niches</span></article>
        <article><strong>$0</strong><span>advance payment on eligible risk-free orders</span></article>
        <article><strong>30 days</strong><span>indexation window under eligible campaign terms</span></article>
        <article><strong>6 months</strong><span>eligible link replacement protection</span></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-section white">
      <div class="shell story-grid">
        <div class="story-sticky" data-reveal><span class="saas-kicker">Why Web Grouth exists</span><h2>Link building needed a lower-risk working model.</h2><p>The agency was shaped around a simple belief: clients should have clarity about the website, terms and live delivery before their budget is committed.</p></div>
        <div class="story-copy" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
          <p>Traditional guest posting often begins with an oversized spreadsheet, unclear publisher relationships and payment before the result can be verified. That creates unnecessary risk for brands and even more operational pressure for agencies managing multiple clients.</p>
          <p>Web Grouth approaches the process differently. We begin with the brief: niche, target URL, anchor, market, metrics and budget. Suitable websites are then selected from a 40,000+ inventory, with important details clarified before the placement moves forward.</p>
          <p>The $0 advance model is the natural result of that approach. For eligible orders, the client receives and verifies the agreed live URL before payment is requested. The goal is not to make unrealistic SEO promises—it is to make fulfilment more transparent and easier to trust.</p>
          <div class="value-grid">
            <article class="value-card"><span>01</span><h3>Human site matching</h3><p>Requirements are reviewed in context instead of relying on one headline metric.</p></article>
            <article class="value-card"><span>02</span><h3>Clear approval</h3><p>Publisher, price, content and placement terms are confirmed before execution.</p></article>
            <article class="value-card"><span>03</span><h3>Verified delivery</h3><p>Completed work is reported through a checkable live URL, not a vague status update.</p></article>
            <article class="value-card"><span>04</span><h3>Repeatable support</h3><p>The workflow supports individual orders, agency fulfilment and recurring campaigns.</p></article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-section navy">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="saas-heading"><span class="saas-kicker">Agency trust factors</span><h2>What trust should look like in practice.</h2><p>Trust is created by the way a campaign is operated—not by badges, stock logos or made-up testimonials.</p></div>
        <div class="trust-grid">
          <article class="trust-card" data-reveal><span>01 · TRANSPARENCY</span><h3>Terms before execution</h3><p>Link type, placement, content, turnaround, pricing and applicable protection are confirmed before work begins.</p></article>
          <article class="trust-card" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1"><span>02 · ACCOUNTABILITY</span><h3>Live-link verification</h3><p>Delivery is tied to a working published URL that can be opened and checked by the client.</p></article>
          <article class="trust-card" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="2"><span>03 · REALISM</span><h3>No ranking guarantees</h3><p>Web Grouth controls the agreed placement workflow, not search-engine rankings or algorithm changes.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-section slate">
      <div class="shell inner-cta" data-reveal><div><span>NEXT STEP</span><h2>Share the brief. Review the sites. Pay after eligible live delivery.</h2></div><a class="saas-button primary" href="/order">Submit your order ↗</a></div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
